WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.250
- So you became a street magician,

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.140
how did this happen?

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.100
At a young age, right?

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.550
- Yes, I was a theater kid.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.090
I started out in theater,

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.220
and my drama teacher, Rob MacIntosh,

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.010
showed me my first magic trick.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.730
Where he took a red silk handkerchief,

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.250
and he stuffed it into his fist.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.740
And when he opened his hand,
the handkerchief was gone.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.810
- It's a classic.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:18.751
- Right, it's a classic.

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.381
You know magic, that's a classic.

00:00:20.381 --> 00:00:22.140
- I love it, and where does it go?

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.690
- Right, so I was hooked.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.350
So I bugged him for two weeks straight.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.760
And then he finally gave me the address,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.830
to Tannen's Magic Shop in New York City.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:29.663
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:29.663 --> 00:00:30.830
- My dad gave me thirty dollars.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.669
I went to the magic shop, and I came home

00:00:32.669 --> 00:00:34.820
with this small red handkerchief,

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.250
and my dad had a heart attack.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:39.260
Cause I spent thirty
dollars on a piece of silk.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.093
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:42.010
I was like, no Dad, I'm
paying for the secret.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.330
So then he was a supporter,

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:46.000
and he's been my strongest
supporter ever since.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.142
- That's so cool.

00:00:47.142 --> 00:00:48.072
(crowd applauds)

00:00:48.072 --> 00:00:48.905
It's something you love.

00:00:48.905 --> 00:00:49.738
- Yeah, I love it, yeah.

00:00:49.738 --> 00:00:53.850
- Do you get a thrill from
watching goofy people like me,

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.500
and that dude, being like, oh my God!

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.071
- It's the best, cause I take,

00:00:58.071 --> 00:01:00.400
with those little tricks,
I used to take them out

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.580
on the streets, performing on the subway,

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.341
in local parks and things like that.

00:01:05.341 --> 00:01:06.174
- Yeah.

00:01:06.174 --> 00:01:07.160
- And then by the time I was 16,

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.440
I was performing in
nightclubs in New York City.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.273
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:01:10.273 --> 00:01:12.840
- So it was like, imagine
I was a variety act,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.781
I would pull out, make birds appear,

00:01:14.781 --> 00:01:16.290
in a burlesque show.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:17.430
A 16 year old. (laughs)

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.730
- I'm just livid they
let a 16 year old in.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.101
This is very Texas.

00:01:21.101 --> 00:01:23.092
(crowd laughs)

00:01:23.092 --> 00:01:24.733
So you have a trick to
show us though, right?

00:01:24.733 --> 00:01:26.443
- Sure, let's try something out.

00:01:26.443 --> 00:01:27.850
- Let's do it!

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.620
- We'll do something with your mind.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.800
- Oh, you don't want to go in there.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.470
(crowd laughs)

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.303
Be aware.

00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:36.136
- Be aware?

00:01:36.136 --> 00:01:37.150
- [Kelly] It's crazy.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:39.512
- This'll probably be
creepy, but really cool.

00:01:39.512 --> 00:01:40.345
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:40.345 --> 00:01:41.780
